# Use-case 06 gap 2 (claim C4) -- FIXED 2026-08-26 by the
# template-clone isolation change (ADR-005): a template instance owns
# its preference's inner value (PrefVal deep `dup` clone), so a rank-2
# default computed from key() answers per generated child.
# Historically the double star was the trigger -- PrefVal.clone shared
# its peg, the one inner key() resolved at the first destination, and
# every child got the first child's key, exit 0 (*key(1)|string,
# *key(1) and plain key(1) escaped only because the rank-1 meet builds
# a fresh pref per destination).
# Pinned in both engines: test/spec/gen-pack.tsv
# pack-rankpref-key-per-child, pack-rankpref-key-override.
# expected: {"out":{"auth":{"value":"auth"},"web":{"value":"web"}},...} exit 0
# actual:   {"out":{"auth":{"value":"auth"},"web":{"value":"web"}},...} exit 0
col: { web: {}, auth: {} }
out: pack($.col, { value: **key(1) | string })
